    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves highlights **Kyle Tucker** (72.68) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) as our primary offensive engines. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Peralta, where his platoon advantage and elite skill profile against a 4.54 xERA arm provide a rock-solid floor. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** is positioned for a breakout performance; his matchup against a vulnerable 6.43 xERA arm, combined with a 14% park factor boost and the leadoff spot, makes him one of our highest-upside plays. **Andy Pages** also merits attention at 68.87, as his specific situational advantage\u2014a slow-delivering opposing pitcher\u2014provides a unique secondary path to secure the stolen bases we prioritize. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a staple in our lineup (63.22), as his ability to mitigate the skill of a tough arm like Greene through a favorable dynamic platoon split keeps his efficiency well within the \"Strong\" range.\n\nWhile the lineup is optimized for daily efficiency, the decision to bench **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.28) was the most difficult call of the morning. Despite his pedigree, his score was suppressed by a poor park factor and a tough matchup against the high-skill arm of Gilbert. Ultimately, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** failed to crack the starting nine because the projections favor the platoon-advantaged **Josh Lowe** and the situational utility of **Andy Pages**. We are closely monitoring the 3.78 xERA of Gray, who faces several of our starters today including **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Lowe**, and **Denzer Guzman**; while the metrics remain stable, this matchup serves as our primary risk factor. We are keeping **Jackson Merrill** active despite a lower score (51.72) due to the volatility of his 7th-place order spot, though we remain confident that our core of **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Drake Baldwin** provides enough depth to sustain our 5x5 categories through the holiday slate.",
